From 216c29b816c875a4a8dd8307a4f2e6ec6242da3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheCryptoDonkey <TheCryptoDonkey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:40:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] feat: enrol several login signers, any one of which
 logs in

Up to five linked signers can now be enrolled for dashboard login, say a
signer at home and one on the phone; there is still one owner. A login
sends the same challenge and code to every enrolled signer whose identity
is still linked, and the first valid approval settles it. A denial,
timeout or offline signer no longer fails the login while another is
still being asked; when all fail, the login reports the most informative
failure (denied, refused, timed out, offline, failed). Later approvals
are ignored.

A login holds the slots of every signer it asked, so a new login is
refused while any of them is busy; enrolling another signer is not held
up. One start still spends one unit of the node-wide budget. The owner's
recent-login history now names the identity whose signer approved.

An approval counts only if its signer is still enrolled and its identity
still linked to the same key when it arrives. Every read-modify-write of
user.json now holds one lock, so enrolments finishing together, or an
enrolment racing a removal, cannot lose or resurrect a signer.
